# Closer Typography (iOS-only)

Source: the Closer typography spec (June 2026) + Apple HIG. Follow these
rules on every screen — new components, edits, audits, refactors.

The canonical role vocabulary lives in `lib/typography.ts`. Reach for the
preset there rather than re-authoring `fontFamily` / `fontWeight` /
`fontSize` / `lineHeight` by hand at each call site.

## Two faces. One job each.

| Face | Where it goes |
| --- | --- |
| **SF Pro** (via `fontFamily: "System"`) | Navigation, tab bar, buttons, cards, the home screen, devotional titles, body copy, section headers, settings, streaks, App Blocks, protection screens. **Everything that's not a reflective quote.** |
| **New York** (via `fontFamily: NEW_YORK` from `lib/typography.ts`) | **Reflective quote moments only.** Scripture callouts, opening reflective quotes, closing reflective quotes, short blockquotes meant to feel like a breath. **Nothing else.** |

New York is the punctuation of the app's voice. Used sparingly it reads
as *special*. Sprinkled across body copy, buttons, or section headers it
collapses into noise. **If you're about to set `fontFamily: NEW_YORK` on
anything other than a quoted scripture or a reflective pull quote, stop.**

### New York is FORBIDDEN on:

- Buttons
- Navigation
- Tab bar
- Form fields and inputs
- Section headers
- Settings rows
- General body text
- Home screen titles
- Eyebrows, labels, captions, statuses

## Role presets (`lib/typography.ts`)

Spread these into a `<Text>` style prop instead of authoring per-call-site
styles. Per-role overrides (a specific color, a tighter margin) compose
cleanly on top via the array form: `style={[typography.body, { color: ink }]}`.

| Role | Face | Weight | Size | Line height | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `typography.pageTitle` | SF Pro | 700 Bold | 40 | 44 | Top-of-screen page anchor (Settings, Library, etc). |
| `typography.devotionalTitle` | SF Pro | 700 Bold | 30 (28–32) | 36 | In-card / in-sermon title for today's reading. |
| `typography.body` | SF Pro | 400 Regular | 17 | 28 | The reading default. iOS body baseline. |
| `typography.button` | SF Pro | 600 Semibold | 17 | — | Primary-action pill label. Single line. |
| `typography.smallLabel` | SF Pro | 600 Semibold | 13 (12–13) | — | All-caps eyebrows, chips, status pills. +0.8 tracking. Caller decides uppercase. |
| `typography.reflectiveQuote` | **New York Italic** | 400 Italic | 26 (24–28) | 36 (34–38) | Centered. The ONLY surface that uses New York. Compose `max-width: 85%` via the parent View. |

## Weights

Apple HIG (verbatim): *"avoid light font weights. Prefer Regular, Medium,
Semibold, or Bold font weights, and avoid Ultralight, Thin, and Light font
weights, which can be difficult to see, especially when text is small."*

| Weight | Use? |
| --- | --- |
| `100` Thin | ❌ FORBIDDEN |
| `200` ExtraLight | ❌ FORBIDDEN |
| `300` Light | ❌ FORBIDDEN |
| `400` Regular | ✅ Default body |
| `500` Medium | ✅ Subtle emphasis |
| `600` Semibold | ✅ Section headers, captions, button labels |
| `700` Bold | ✅ Titles, primary actions |
| `800` ExtraBold | ✅ Hero only (use sparingly) |
| `900` Black | ✅ Allowed but rarely needed |

In SF Pro, weights are reached via the `fontWeight` property — NEVER by
stringifying a face name. `fontFamily: "System", fontWeight: "700"` is
correct; legacy `"PlusJakartaSans_700Bold"` is gone and must not return.

## Sizes

Use the 8pt grid: 11, 12, 13, 15, 17, 20, 22, 28, 30, 34, 40, 48…

| Context | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| **Body text** | 17pt default. The iOS-baseline. |
| **Minimum size** | **11pt floor.** Anything below 11pt MUST be raised. |
| **Reflective quote** | 24–28pt. The serif italic needs scale to land. |

Avoid stair-stepping outside the 8pt grid unless replacing a fixed Apple
system size (e.g. SF Symbols small chips at 12 or 13).

## Alignment

- **Left-align** body text. Never justify on iOS (Apple-HIG-forbidden).
- Reflective quotes are centered by default (`typography.reflectiveQuote`
  carries `textAlign: "center"`).
- Center-align is otherwise reserved for compositional moments: hero
  titles, prayer beats, splash/launch states, standalone captions under
  hero artwork.

## Color & Contrast

- Body text on dark surfaces: target **AAA 7:1** contrast (≈ `#CCCCCC` on
  `#000` / `#151515`). AA 4.5:1 is the absolute floor.
- Never use color alone to convey meaning. Pair every color cue with
  shape, weight, or icon (e.g. `shield.fill` vs `shield` outline for
  protection state).

## Touch Targets

- Every interactive element needs at minimum a **44×44pt hit area**. If
  the visual element is smaller, extend with `hitSlop`.

## Dynamic Type

- Prefer `allowFontScaling` (default-on) for narrative copy so users with
  Larger Text accommodations get the scale.
- Only opt out (`allowFontScaling={false}`) for tightly composed hero
  typography where scaling would break layout — and only after
  considering the accessibility tradeoff.

## Concrete examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — 9pt is below the HIG 11pt floor; legacy PlusJakartaSans face.
<Text style={{ fontSize: 9, fontFamily: "PlusJakartaSans_300Light" }}>…</Text>

// ✅ GOOD — uses the body role token, leaves family + weight to the system.
import { typography } from "@/lib/typography";
<Text style={typography.body}>…</Text>

// ✅ GOOD — small-caps eyebrow via the smallLabel preset + uppercase.
<Text
  style={[typography.smallLabel, { textTransform: "uppercase" }]}
>
  DAY STREAK
</Text>

// ✅ GOOD — primary-action pill label.
<Text style={[typography.button, { color: "#FFFFFF" }]}>Read Now</Text>

// ✅ GOOD — reflective scripture quote (the ONLY New York Italic spot).
<Text style={typography.reflectiveQuote}>
  &ldquo;The Lord is my shepherd; I shall not want.&rdquo;
</Text>

// ❌ BAD — New York Italic on a button. Forbidden.
<Text
  style={{ fontFamily: NEW_YORK, fontStyle: "italic", fontSize: 17 }}
>
  Continue
</Text>

// ❌ BAD — justified body copy.
<Text style={{ textAlign: "justify" }}>…</Text>
```

## Reviewer checklist

Before shipping any screen edit, scan for:

- [ ] No `fontFamily: "PlusJakartaSans_*"` anywhere (the legacy face is
      gone; the codebase lives on `"System"` and `NEW_YORK`).
- [ ] No `NEW_YORK` outside a reflective-quote surface (scripture
      callouts, pull quotes). It is FORBIDDEN on buttons, nav, tab bar,
      form fields, section headers, settings, body text, or any home
      screen title.
- [ ] No `fontSize` below 11.
- [ ] No `fontWeight: "100" | "200" | "300"`.
- [ ] No `textAlign: "justify"`.
- [ ] Body text 17pt where reading-density matters.
- [ ] All `Pressable` / `TouchableOpacity` ≥ 44×44pt (or `hitSlop`
      compensates).
- [ ] All color signals paired with a non-color channel.
